{"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/multidimensionalScalingLayout(edgeLength:maxIterations:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A drawing by classical multidimensional scaling of the shortest-path distances: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"coordinates of the best rank-2 approximation of the doubly centred squared distances."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph\/multidimensionalscalinglayout(edgelength:maxiterations:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"multidimensionalScalingLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeLength","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":" = { _ in 1 }, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","text":"NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The distance d_ij of two vertices is their shortest-path distance with "},{"code":"edgeLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (hops by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default); between components it is 1 + L̄·√n, L̄ the mean edge length, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"stressMajorizationLayout()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". With B = −½ J D⁽²⁾ J (D⁽²⁾ the squared distances, J the centring"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matrix), x is √λ₁ · v₁ and y is √λ₂ · v₂ for the two largest eigenvalues λ₁ ≥ λ₂ of B and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their unit eigenvectors (a negative eigenvalue gives 0). When the distances are Euclidean"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the plane, the drawing reproduces them exactly, up to a rigid motion. Each axis’s sign"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes its first entry, in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, whose magnitude is at least 10⁻⁴ of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"largest positive. The drawing is centred on the origin. A directed graph is drawn through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"undirectedView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Torgerson, “Multidimensional scaling: I. Theory and method”, Psychometrika 17(4), 1952.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n·(n + m)) for the distances by breadth-first search (O(n·m log n) by Dijkstra when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lengths differ), then O(n³) for the dense eigensystem; n² "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every edge length is positive and finite; "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least 1."}]}],"name":"Precondition","style":"note","type":"aside"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" after ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" QL iterations in all (30 n when nil), as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"spectralLayout(weight:maxIterations:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Throws","style":"note","type":"aside"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GraphDrawing","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"role":"symbol","title":"multidimensionalScalingLayout(edgeLength:maxIterations:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"multidimensionalScalingLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"edgeLength"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"prec